  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a positive integer MMM and an array A&nbsp;(1≤Ai≤M)A \\ (1\\leq A_i \\leq M)A&nbsp;(1≤Ai​≤M) consisting of NNN positive integers.\n\nFind the **lexicographically largest** array BBB such that:\n\n\n∣B∣=N|B|=N∣B∣=N;\n1≤Bi≤M1 \\leq B_i \\leq M1≤Bi​≤M for all 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N;\nAi=gcd⁡(B1,B2,…,Bi)A_i = \\gcd(B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_i)Ai​=gcd(B1​,B2​,…,Bi​), where gcd⁡\\gcdgcd denotes the greatest common divisor.\nNote that the input AAA guarantees that BBB always exists.\n\nFor two arrays XXX and YYY, both of size NNN, the array XXX is said to be lexicographically larger than array YYY, if, in the first position where XXX and YYY differ, Xi&gt;YiX_i \\gt Y_iXi​&gt;Yi​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space separated integers NNN and MMM — the  length of array AAA and upper bound on array elements.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ representing the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the lexicographically largest array BBB, satisfying the given conditions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1041 \\leq N \\leq 10^41≤N≤104",
      "1≤M≤1091 \\leq M \\leq 10^91≤M≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1045 \\cdot 10^45⋅104."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
